actual_output:
Based on the information provided in the context, the following government entities are mandated to comply with the revised Dearness Allowance rates:

1. All Regional Offices;
2. US(FD-I/A)/US(FD-I/B)/SO(FD-I/A)/SO(FD-I/B), with the request to take further action in the matter;
3. CU/DU/DC/IUC Sections, with a request to take further necessary action at their end;
4. UGC e-Office;
5. UGC website.

These entities are specifically mentioned as recipients of the circular and are requested to take further necessary or action as required.

The Under Secretary (Admn.) is responsible for taking further necessary action on the Dearness Allowance revision within the University Grants Commission. The circular is to be copied to:

1. All Regional Offices;
2. US(FD-I A)/US(I/B)/FD-III/SO(FD-I/A/SO(FD-I/B)/FD-III), with the request to take further action in the matter;
3. CU/DU/DC/IUC Sections, with a request to take further necessary action at their end.

Additionally, copies are to be sent to UGC e-Office and UGC website.
